# Unified Packed UI Scene — full-schema exact-size emitter (Phase 2, lane L4).
#
# Design authority: `doc/05_design/ui/unified_packed_ui_scene.md` §2, §5.
# Plan: `doc/03_plan/ui/unified_packed_ui_scene_agent_lanes.md` (L4).
#
# `draw_ir_v3_emit.spl` (Kernels A-E) stays untouched as the CPU-reference
# oracle for tables 0-2/3/4/6/7 (COMMANDS/GEOMETRY/PAINT/TEXT_RUNS/GLYPHS/
# PATH_SPANS/PATH_POINTS) — it never populates RESOURCES, CLIPS, TRANSFORMS,
# HIT_SHAPES or PROVENANCE_EDGES (Kernel D always writes
# `draw_ir_v3_empty_resource_table()` etc for those). This file is a NEW,
# additive emitter that counts and writes ALL SIXTEEN `UiSceneTableId` tables
# via the L1 `ui_scene_scan` / `ui_scene_verify` state machine (design §5),
# enforcing exact emitted == counted per table with Deficit/Surplus receipts
# on mismatch (never a silent clamp), overflow receipts on capacity breach
# (nothing emitted, front generation untouched), and stable component-id
# allocation. Uses the `UiSceneCapacityExtensionV1` sidecar for capacity —
# the frozen `gpu_web_capacity_manifest.spl` is never touched.
#
# Scope note: this lane is the single-generation CPU-reference emitter only.
# Multi-producer arena sharing, front/back generations and bounds-checked
# native writers over a persistent session arena are lane L5's job
# (`src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/ui/ui_scene_arena.spl`,
# `draw_ir_v3_native_writer.spl`) — this file has no arena and no session
# state, matching design §1's tier table ("Pure count/scan/verify/emit over
# value buffers; the CPU oracle path").

use common.ui.draw_ir_v3.{
